{"id":"the-black-christ-and-other-poems","title":"The Black Christ and Other Poems","author":"Countee Cullen","year":"1929","note":"Harlem lyrics and a long lynching passion — Cullen at full cry.","minutes":238,"cover":"","coverAlt":"","scenes":[{"id":"s0","title":"Chapter 1","place":"Chapter 1","reentry":"That Bright Chimeric Beast","prompt":"What does the poem demand of you?"},{"id":"s1","title":"Chapter II","place":"Chapter II","reentry":"II","prompt":"What does the poem demand of you?"}],"breaths":[{"id":"s0-0","sceneId":"s0","text":"That Bright Chimeric Beast"},{"id":"s0-1","sceneId":"s0","text":"(For Lynn Riggs)"},{"id":"s0-2","sceneId":"s0","text":"That bright chimeric beast"},{"id":"s0-3","sceneId":"s0","text":"Conceived yet never born,"},{"id":"s0-4","sceneId":"s0","text":"Save in the poet’s breast,"},{"id":"s0-5","sceneId":"s0","text":"The white-flanked unicorn,"},{"id":"s0-6","sceneId":"s0","text":"Never may be shaken"},{"id":"s0-7","sceneId":"s0","text":"From his solitude;"},{"id":"s0-8","sceneId":"s0","text":"Never may be taken"},{"id":"s0-9","sceneId":"s0","text":"In any earthly wood."},{"id":"s0-10","sceneId":"s0","text":"That bird forever feathered,"},{"id":"s0-11","sceneId":"s0","text":"Of its new self the sire,"},{"id":"s0-12","sceneId":"s0","text":"After aeons weathered,"},{"id":"s0-13","sceneId":"s0","text":"Reincarnate by fire,"},{"id":"s0-14","sceneId":"s0","text":"Falcon may not nor eagle"},{"id":"s0-15","sceneId":"s0","text":"Swerve from his eerie,"},{"id":"s0-16","sceneId":"s0","text":"Nor any crumb inveigle"},{"id":"s0-17","sceneId":"s0","text":"Down to an earthly tree."},{"id":"s0-18","sceneId":"s0","text":"That fish of the dread regime"},{"id":"s0-19","sceneId":"s0","text":"Invented to become"},{"id":"s0-20","sceneId":"s0","text":"The fable and the dream"},{"id":"s0-21","sceneId":"s0","text":"Of the Lord’s aquarium,"},{"id":"s0-22","sceneId":"s0","text":"Leviathan, the jointed"},{"id":"s0-23","sceneId":"s0","text":"IO"},{"id":"s0-24","sceneId":"s0","text":"Harpoon was never wrought"},{"id":"s0-25","sceneId":"s0","text":"By which the Lord’s anointed"},{"id":"s0-26","sceneId":"s0","text":"Will suffer to be caught."},{"id":"s0-27","sceneId":"s0","text":"Bird of the deathless breast,"},{"id":"s0-28","sceneId":"s0","text":"Fish of the frantic fin,"},{"id":"s0-29","sceneId":"s0","text":"That bright chimeric beast"},{"id":"s0-30","sceneId":"s0","text":"Flashing the argent skin,—"},{"id":"s0-31","sceneId":"s0","text":"If beasts like these you’d harry,"},{"id":"s0-32","sceneId":"s0","text":"Plumb then the poet’s dream;"},{"id":"s0-33","sceneId":"s0","text":"Make it your aviary,"},{"id":"s0-34","sceneId":"s0","text":"Make it your wood and stream."},{"id":"s0-35","sceneId":"s0","text":"There only shall the swish"},{"id":"s0-36","sceneId":"s0","text":"Be heard, of the regal fish;"},{"id":"s0-37","sceneId":"s0","text":"There like a golden knife"},{"id":"s0-38","sceneId":"s0","text":"Dart the feet of the unicorn,"},{"id":"s0-39","sceneId":"s0","text":"And there, death brought to life,"},{"id":"s0-40","sceneId":"s0","text":"The dead bird be reborn."},{"id":"s1-0","sceneId":"s1","text":"II"},{"id":"s1-1","sceneId":"s1","text":"At the Etoile"},{"id":"s1-2","sceneId":"s1","text":"(At the Unknown Soldier’s Grave in Paris)"},{"id":"s1-3","sceneId":"s1","text":"If in the lists of life he bore him well,"},{"id":"s1-4","sceneId":"s1","text":"Sat gracefully or fell unhorsed in love,"},{"id":"s1-5","sceneId":"s1","text":"No tongue is dowered now with speech to"},{"id":"s1-6","sceneId":"s1","text":"tell"},{"id":"s1-7","sceneId":"s1","text":"Since he and death somewhere matched glove"},{"id":"s1-8","sceneId":"s1","text":"with glove."},{"id":"s1-9","sceneId":"s1","text":"What proud or humble union gave him birth,"},{"id":"s1-10","sceneId":"s1","text":"Not reckoning on this immortal bed,"},{"id":"s1-11","sceneId":"s1","text":"Is one more riddle that the cryptic earth"},{"id":"s1-12","sceneId":"s1","text":"Though knowing chooses to retain unsaid."},{"id":"s1-13","sceneId":"s1","text":"Since he was weak as other men,—or like"},{"id":"s1-14","sceneId":"s1","text":"Young Galahad as fair in thought as limb,"},{"id":"s1-15","sceneId":"s1","text":"Each bit of moving dust in France may strike"},{"id":"s1-16","sceneId":"s1","text":"Its breast in pride, knowing he stands for"},{"id":"s1-17","sceneId":"s1","text":"him."},{"id":"s1-18","sceneId":"s1","text":"1"},{"id":"s1-19","sceneId":"s1","text":"Two Epitaphs"},{"id":"s1-20","sceneId":"s1","text":"1   For the Unknown Soldier (Paris)"},{"id":"s1-21","sceneId":"s1","text":"Unknown but not unhonored rest,"},{"id":"s1-22","sceneId":"s1","text":"Symbol of all Time shall not reap;"},{"id":"s1-23","sceneId":"s1","text":"Not one stilled heart in that torn breast,"},{"id":"s1-24","sceneId":"s1","text":"But a myriad millions sleep."},{"id":"s1-25","sceneId":"s1","text":"2 For a Child Still-born"},{"id":"s1-26","sceneId":"s1","text":"Here sleeps a spark that never burned,"},{"id":"s1-27","sceneId":"s1","text":"A seed not granted spring to bloom,"},{"id":"s1-28","sceneId":"s1","text":"A soul whose darkened pathway"},{"id":"s1-29","sceneId":"s1","text":"turned"},{"id":"s1-30","sceneId":"s1","text":"From tomb of flesh to dusty tomb."},{"id":"s1-31","sceneId":"s1","text":"14"},{"id":"s1-32","sceneId":"s1","text":"To an Unknown Poet"},{"id":"s1-33","sceneId":"s1","text":"OVE is enough,” I read somewhere;"},{"id":"s1-34","sceneId":"s1","text":"Lines some poor poet in his pride"},{"id":"s1-35","sceneId":"s1","text":"And poverty wrote on the air"},{"id":"s1-36","sceneId":"s1","text":"To ease his heart, and soothe his bride."},{"id":"s1-37","sceneId":"s1","text":"Something in me, child of an age"},{"id":"s1-38","sceneId":"s1","text":"Cold to the core, undeified,"},{"id":"s1-39","sceneId":"s1","text":"Warmed to my brother bard, this sage;"},{"id":"s1-40","sceneId":"s1","text":"And I too leaned upon my pride."},{"id":"s1-41","sceneId":"s1","text":"But pride I found can blind our eyes,"},{"id":"s1-42","sceneId":"s1","text":"And poverty is worse than pride."},{"id":"s1-43","sceneId":"s1","text":"Love’s breed from both is a nest of lies;"},{"id":"s1-44","sceneId":"s1","text":"And singer of sweet songs, you lied."},{"id":"s1-45","sceneId":"s1","text":"15"},{"id":"s1-46","sceneId":"s1","text":"Little Sonnet to Little"},{"id":"s1-47","sceneId":"s1","text":"Friends"},{"id":"s1-48","sceneId":"s1","text":"ET not the proud of heart condemn"},{"id":"s1-49","sceneId":"s1","text":"Me that I mould my ways to hers,"},{"id":"s1-50","sceneId":"s1","text":"Groping for healing in a hem"},{"id":"s1-51","sceneId":"s1","text":"No wind of passion ever stirs;"},{"id":"s1-52","sceneId":"s1","text":"Nor let them sweetly pity me"},{"id":"s1-53","sceneId":"s1","text":"When I am out of sound and sight;"},{"id":"s1-54","sceneId":"s1","text":"They waste their time and energy;"}]}